21. GPU  hub

Which graphics chip you have, which driver runs it, and whether programs can use
it.

On your machine
  card0     Intel, driver i915, shows the boot screen
  Screens   eDP-1 1920x1200 · free: DP-1, HDMI-A-1
  Compute   /dev/dri/renderD128

Commands
  lspci -k | grep -A3 -E 'VGA|3D'
                          GPUs and the kernel driver each uses
  glxinfo -B              OpenGL renderer: your GPU, or llvmpipe for software
                          (mesa-utils)
  vulkaninfo --summary    Vulkan devices and drivers
  nvidia-smi              NVIDIA: use, memory, processes, driver and CUDA
                          version
  echo $XDG_SESSION_TYPE  wayland or x11

Paths
  /sys/class/drm/  graphics cards and their screen outputs
  /dev/dri/        card* to drive screens, renderD* to draw and compute

Cards
  idk 5.1  What a GPU does differently
  idk 5.2  GPU drivers: the kernel, Mesa and NVIDIA
  idk 5.3  How a picture reaches the screen: KMS, Wayland and X11
  idk 5.4  Computing on the GPU, and when your program can't see it
